{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779150191,"nonce":"sVWLaZT/uBa3zq6xuxojSVOavWA=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABCqP3Nw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/130","origin":"github"},"title":"Field validation: over-horizon Starlink-only operation","message":"## Goal\n\nValidate that BizzyBoat can operate over Starlink/VPN only, as required for\nover-horizon survey work. The 2026-05-01 deployment ran with WiFi continuously\navailable; we have no field data on Starlink-only behaviour, and the bandwidth\ncharacteristics of the two paths are very different.\n\nPart of #124 (post-mission review §1.3 / §1.4).\n\n## What we know\n\nFrom the 2026-05-01 deployment + 2026-05-18 pier calibration (analysis notes in\n`~/data/analysis/2026-05-01_findings.md` and `2026-05-18_starlink_only_budget.md`):\n\n| | WiFi | Starlink/VPN |\n|---|---|---|\n| Configured cap | 12 Mbps | 8 Mbps |\n| Pier-measured ceiling | ≥30 Mbps UDP @ 0% loss | ~20 Mbps with ≥1.4% loss; ~5 Mbps clean |\n| Avg RTT | 9 ms | 65 ms (via bencloud WireGuard) |\n| Loss character | clean | structurally lossy at every offered rate |\n\nTotal VPN demand during 2026-05-01: **~2.75 Mbps average** (mostly cameras), with\n**40+ Mbps keyframe peaks**. Operational essentials (heartbeat / mission /\nmavros / odom / tf / diagnostics / plan) sum to **~0.4 Mbps** — well within\nStarlink's clean budget at any range.\n\n## What we don't know\n\n1. How Starlink behaves under sustained moderate load over minutes\n   (satellite-handoff burst-loss events; 15 s iperf3 windows hide them).\n2. How `udp_bridge` behaves when WiFi disappears mid-mission (we never tested\n   that explicitly).\n3. How the existing `udp_bridge` recovers (or doesn't) from a forced 30–60 s\n   Starlink outage — the deployment did see one ~3 min outage at 14:28 EDT\n   that's worth back-testing once the resend rework lands.\n\n## Proposed work\n\n### 1. Sustained Starlink UDP characterization\n\n`iperf3 -u -t 600 -b 5M -l 1400` and `-b 1M` boat→shore over the VPN target IP.\nCaptures burst-loss events that short tests miss. Compare loss percentage and\nloss-event duration distribution against the deployment's per-topic outage\ncatalog.\n\n### 2. Add a Starlink-only profile to `bizzyboat.yaml`\n\nExplicit configuration that turns off WiFi-side topics and restricts the VPN\n`topics_list` to:\n\n- All operational essentials (heartbeat, mission_manager, platforms, odom, tf,\n  mavros, diagnostics, plan, path_follower_visualization, hover_visualization).\n- **At most one** camera ffmpeg stream (operator's choice — forward by default).\n- Segmentation overlays optional.\n\nToday's config defaults to \"everything everywhere\"; the Starlink-only mode\nshould be a single-flag switch (separate launch arg or config profile), not a\nhand-edited per-deployment change.\n\n### 3. Keyframe-stagger config on OAK encoders\n\nThe 14–20 Mbps single-second peaks per camera are H.264/H.265 IDR keyframes.\nThree cameras keyframing simultaneously can produce 30–40 Mbps spikes (which\nis exactly what the §1.1 starboard 1.06 MB/s peak drop in 2026-05-01 was).\nOffset the three cameras' GOP starts by ⅓ GOP each. Bitrate-neutral; just\ndecorrelates the spikes.\n\n### 4. WiFi-disabled bench rehearsal\n\nBoat on the pier. WiFi administratively down at the boat MikroTik (or\n`udp_bridge` started with WiFi connection disabled in config). Verify:\n\n- All essential topics flow on VPN as expected.\n- A forced ~30 s `bencloud` outage doesn't permanently brick the bridge.\n- After bencloud comes back, every topic resumes within a defined recovery\n  window.\n\n### 5. Short-hop survey rehearsal in Starlink-only profile\n\n200 m hop, line of sight to operator, recover. Compare per-topic outage budget\nagainst the 2026-05-01 deployment. This is the field validation that gates\n\"over-horizon survey is operationally safe.\"\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `udp_bridge` resend-layer rework (in progress; not blocking this work since\n  much of it is config + profile-level).\n- `bencloud` reachability needs to be verified separately as part of this\n  effort — it's the dominant VPN latency hop (35 ms of 65 ms RTT) and a single\n  point of failure for Starlink-only operation.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Sustained-load UDP characterization captured; loss-event distribution\n      documented in `~/data/analysis/`.\n- [ ] Starlink-only profile lands in `bizzyboat.yaml`, exercised in tests.\n- [ ] Keyframe staggering configured; measured peak reduction documented.\n- [ ] WiFi-disabled bench rehearsal: every essential topic flows; recovery\n      from forced 30 s outage characterized.\n- [ ] Short-hop survey rehearsal completed with the Starlink-only profile;\n      per-topic outage budget meets or beats the 2026-05-01 deployment baseline.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- udp_bridge resend mechanism redesign — being handled separately.\n- Multi-camera-over-Starlink full-bandwidth case — current configuration\n  already saturates; the goal is *minimum viable Starlink-only operation*, not\n  \"ship the same operator UX over Starlink\".\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}